      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}: I include the avatar's version number at the end of the name so I know which avatar version I am wearing. However, since the menu doesn't update the name correctly, the avatar's actual version number doesn't match the avatar's version number in the name. It will show the old name and sometimes show the new version. \n\nWhen debugging something on an avatar, how will I know if my bugfix worked or if I'm simply viewing an old avatar version? There is no way to confirm which version of the avatar you are actually wearing. \n\nTo get around this issue, whenever I update an avatar and I need to know that I am indeed viewing the latest avatar version, I will change the color of the avatar's hair. That way, if the hair color is the old color then I know I am looking at the old avatar in game.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-02-27T20:22:57.856Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If I upload an avatar to a fresh blueprint ID, it won't show up in the new menu system until I restart the client or wait a _very_ long time. \n\nIf I update an avatar to an existing blueprint ID, the menu won't update the _name_ of the avatar, however, it will update the avatar actually being used. This is confusing since the menu will show the name for the _old_ version of the avatar yet it will typically load the latest avatar version. \n\nIt's frustrating and more difficult to debug avatars when the name shown for the avatar in the menu doesn't match the name of the avatar actually being worn.",
